{#
 # The front page an application has before it has one of its own.
 #
 # Served by the shared module's "/" route. It is meant to be replaced, and
 # there are two ways to do that without editing the framework: change this
 # file, or declare a "/" route in a module of your own. Every other module
 # registers after the shared one, so its route is the one that answers.
 #
 # Nothing here names a directory on disk as a URL, and nothing here says which
 # version is running: a default page is public by definition, and it has no
 # business telling a stranger what to look up in a changelog.
 #}
{% extends "layout.twig" %}

{% block title %}Welcome{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">It works</p>
    <h1>Your application is running</h1>
    <p>No module has claimed the front page yet, so this is the default template's home page.</p>
</section>

<section class="next">
    <h2>Where to go from here</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
        <li>
            <strong>Add a module.</strong>
            A directory under <code>modules/Plugins/</code> with a <code>module.php</code> in it is discovered on
            its own. Its routes, hooks, filters, commands and schedules are declared there.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Claim this page.</strong>
            Declare a <code>/</code> route in your module, or edit <code>templates/home.twig</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Check the wiring.</strong>
            <code>php laika module:list</code> and <code>php laika route:list</code> show what was
            discovered and what answers.
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>
{% endblock %}
